            "source_snippet": "import sys\n\ndef min_performance_duration(a, b, c, d):\n    # Sort the initial positions to simplify calculations\n    positions = sorted([a, b, c])\n    a, b, c = positions[0], positions[1], positions[2]\n    \n    # Calculate the initial distances between pairs\n    dist_ab = b - a\n    dist_bc = c - b\n    \n    # If the distances are already sufficient, return 0\n    if dist_ab >= d and dist_bc >= d:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Calculate the minimum steps needed to satisfy the conditions\n    steps = 0\n    \n    # Move the middle person (b) to ensure dist_ab >= d\n    if dist_ab < d:\n        steps += d - dist_ab\n        b += d - dist_ab\n    \n    # Recalculate the distances after moving b\n    dist_ab = b - a\n    dist_bc = c - b\n    \n    # Move the outer persons (a and c) to ensure dist_bc >= d\n    if dist_bc < d:\n        steps += d - dist_bc\n        c += d - dist_bc\n    \n    return steps\n\n# Read input\ninput = sys.stdin.read\ndata = input().split()\na = int(data[0])\nb = int(data[1])\nc = int(data[2])\nd = int(data[3])\n\n# Calculate and print the result\nresult = min_performance_duration(a, b, c, d)\nprint(result)",
